      "problem": "Factor the expression $3{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Note that all of the terms have a common factor of $x.$ To simplify the computation, we can factor out the $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-x & =x(3{x}^{2}+2x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we factor the polynomial $3{x}^{2}+2x-1,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(3{x}^{2}+2x-1) & = \\\\ x((3{x}^{2}+3x)+(-x-1)) & = \\\\ x(3x(x+1)-1(x+1)) & = \\\\ x(3x-1)(x+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
